Ejecutivo de ventas senior responsable de elaborar el plan de acción para ventas activas y la prospección de nuevos negocios, con el fin de cumplir con el plan de negocio definido para el área de ventas técnicas de proyectos, actualizaciones y/o modernizaciones, repuestos y planes de mantenimiento.

Responsibilities / Tasks

• Gestionar una cartera de clientes clave, manteniendo relaciones a largo plazo y detectando y maximizando oportunidades de venta mediante el desarrollo de estrategias y planes de acción;

• Prospectar, elaborar y negociar presupuestos, ofreciendo las mejores condiciones, precios y plazos con el fin de fidelizar a los clientes e impulsar las ventas;

• Atender a los clientes en general, resolviendo dudas y asistiendo en la venta del portafolio de productos;

• Negociar internamente precios, plazos y descuentos para ofrecer la mejor atención al cliente final;

• Analizar la base instalada actual y futura, identificar oportunidades de negocio y determinar el potencial de mercado;

• Visitar clientes (hasta el 80% del tiempo) en todo el territorio nacional;

• Desarrollar acciones y planes de mercado para fortalecer e incrementar el volumen de negocio;

• Alinear estrategias y acciones con la casa matriz y otras filiales del grupo GEA (clientes globales, oportunidades, requisitos del mercado, etc.); Realizar el seguimiento de los objetivos y resultados de ventas para garantizar el cumplimiento de las metas de ventas y rentabilidad;

• Negociar condiciones comerciales y técnicas para lograr el mayor beneficio para la empresa, cumpliendo al mismo tiempo con las expectativas de clientes, proveedores, la dirección y la casa matriz;

• Generar sinergias mediante la integración con otras empresas del grupo;

• Actuar como enlace en las negociaciones de contratos legales con el cliente (con el apoyo del departamento jurídico);

• Elaborar informes internos (sobre proyectos en curso, así como operaciones ganadas o perdidas bajo su responsabilidad directa);

• Participar en ferias comerciales y seminarios;

Your Profile / Qualifications

• Experiencia en ventas industriales B2B en fabricantes de bienes de capital, preferentemente en el área de servicios.

• Formación superior en ingeniería química, ingeniería de alimentos, ingeniería de automatización o ingeniería mecánica.

• Idiomas: Inglés avanzado

• Otras cualificaciones/Adicional:

• Experiencia en ventas de equipos y sistemas de procesamiento; conocimiento de sistemas ERP

• Habilidades interpersonales:

• Habilidades de negociación.

• Trabajo en equipo.

• Enfoque en el cliente.

• Enfoque en resultados .

• Flexibilidad.

• Organización.

• Comunicación .

• Dinamismo.

• Proactividad.

• Relaciones interpersonales.

Did we spark your interest?

Then please click apply above to access our guided application process.

À propos de l’entreprise

Créée en 1961 à Calais , la Société Calaisienne de Réparation Navale et Mécanique, SOCARENAM s’installe également en 1969 à Boulogne sur Mer , en 1973 à Dunkerque , en 2009 à Saint Malo et en 2015 à Etaples .

Aujourd’hui, ce sont près de 250 collaborateurs répartis au sein de 6 entités et filiales qui assurent nos 3 activités majeures : la construction navale, la réparation navale et la transformation de navires, la chaudronnerie industrielle et la mécanique.

Avec une expérience de plus de 60 ans au service d’une clientèle exigeante, nous savons nous adapter pour répondre aux besoins spécifiques des armateurs.

Nos équipes sont composées d’ingénieurs, de techniciens spécialisés, d’ouvriers qualifiés et agréés par les organismes de contrôle. Nous sommes parmi les chantiers les plus performants au niveau national et international. Plus de 300 navires sont à ce jour sortis de nos ateliers.

Vous connaissez le secteur de la construction navale ou souhaitez le découvrir ?

Venez rejoindre une activité atypique menée par une équipe de passionnés !

Voir la fiche de l'entreprise

Description Des Activités Significatives De L'emploi

En lien étroit avec la Direction Générale de la société, vous facilitez l’organisation quotidienne et jouez le rôle d’interface entre la direction et les autres services, les clients et les partenaires. Vos missions :

Gestion D’Agenda Et De Planning

• Planification des rendez-vous ;

• Organisation des réunions ;

• Organisation des déplacements professionnels en France et à l’international ;

• Traiter les demandes urgentes en garantissant la confidentialité.

Secréatariat De Haut Niveau

• Rédiger, mettre en forme et suivre les courriers ;

• Préparation de dossiers et mise en forme de présentation ;

• Préparation / mise en forme des offres commerciales en lien avec les services transverses.

Suivi De Projet & Gestion Adminsitrative

• Participation à des dossiers transverses ;

• Commande des prestations en lien avec ses activités ;

• Assistance au suivi administratif des dossiers ;

• Suivi budgétaire de ses activités en lien avec la comptabilité.

Interface, Évènementiel & Communication

• Accueil physique et téléphonique (clients, délégations officielles, partenaires,...) ;

• Transmission de l’information et des consignes ;

• Représentation de la Direction auprès des interlocuteurs internes & externes ;

• Organiser, préparer et participer aux salons & évènements professionnels de l’entreprise (Logistique, prestataires, budgets…) ;

• Préparer les dossiers de presse et de communication internes / externes.

Profil

• Expérience d’environ 5 ans sur une fonction polyvalente, idéalement auprès d’une direction ;

• Très bonne maîtrise des outils bureaucratiques et collaboratifs (Word, Excel, Powerpoint et Outlook) ;

• Excellente expression orale, écrite et orthographe rigoureuse ;

• Maîtrise de l’anglais professionnel ;

• Savoir être : discrétion, autonomie, rigueur, sens de l’organisation, réactivité, diplomatie, sens du service.

Voir la fiche métier : Assistant de direction (H/F)

Be part of Mindray

Mindray is a Chinese multinational manufacturer of medical instruments with headquartered in Shenzhen, Guangdong. The company designs and produces medical equipment and accessories, with presence in more than 190 countries and regions, with a strong commitment with research and development. Our mission is focus on Advance medical technologies to make healthcare more accessible.

With Mindray as Marketing Specialist - Medical Imaging your main responsabilities will be:

• Provide technical support and training to regional sales and distributors;

• Coordinate with R&D to ensure the product are suitable for the regional market;

• Design competitive strategy and give advice to sales on international business;

• Collect and analyze marketing information and sales data to understand and meet customer requirements;

• Organize and participate in exhibitions, seminars and to give advice on product promotion materials in the market region.

Requirements

• Bachelor degree or above, majoring in engineering or equivalent, bio-medical, human science or related disciplines;

• Above 2 years’ experience in medical imaging product extend and technical service

• Excellent command of written & spoken English;

• Previous experience in life support medical devices field

• Willingness to travel

Location: Buenos Aires

We Are

RTB House is a global company that provides state-of-the-art marketing technologies for top brands and agencies worldwide. Its proprietary ad-buying engine is the first in the world to be powered entirely by Deep Learning algorithms, enabling advertisers to generate outstanding results and reach their goals at every stage of the funnel.

Founded in 2012 and now operating in 90+ markets, RTB House has always been private-by-design. It embraces first-party advertising and a relentless approach to innovation. RTB House offers end-to-end Deep Learning-powered AdTech products and solutions to maximize conversion, drive new customer acquisition, create engagement, and fuel long-term demand for a global base of clients.

In 2026, RTB House launched rtb.com, a self-service platform specifically designed to allow small and medium-sized businesses and agencies to deploy auto-built creatives and maximize performance on any budget.

You Will

• cooperation with brands from the e-commerce market in Cono Sur;

• managing a portfolio of clients independently;

• negotiating business terms and doing upsell;

• regular performance reporting to clients;

• regular face to face meetings with clients to ensure premium customer service;

• execute customer communications – personally and via telephone, video-calls or email, in line with standards and processes;

• respond to customer requests and inquiries in a professional and timely manner;

• responsible for customer success and long-term relationship;

• provide specific information regarding company’s services and products;

• assist customers in the process of launching ad campaigns;

• develop and maintain in-depth product knowledge;

• data improvement and optimization;

• contributing to company-wide or local projects in account management.

Desired Experience

• Experience with account management and dealing with large clients

• Experience with programmatic/retargeting

• Persuasive communication, experience in negotiations and presentations

• Strong problem solving skills, quantitative skills, very good command of Excel

• Good track record, success cases in the previous role(s)

• Strong and clear motivation, being able to self-motivate

• Available to go to the office in buenos aires twice a week

• Native in Spanish with fluency in English

• Availability to travel 5-15%.

We Offer

• Opportunity to gain experience in the field of RTB House, the fastest growing, thriving area of online advertising;

• Competitive salary in USD;

• A chance to be a part of a team that shapes the future of online marketing globally;

• Opportunity to work in a truly international environment.

Apply now!

You don't need to tick every box to apply. If you are passionate about digital marketing, send us your CV, and we'll review it.

Information for Applicants: Argentina

Your daily life will be focusing around:

• Analyze, gather and document business & functional requirements (Product Vision, Roadmap, Product Backlog);

• Collaborate with business, developers and QA through all phases of the product development lifecycle (e.g. scoping, gathering requirements, design, development, QA, deployment) to deliver the best quality products;

• Manage the Product Backlog prioritization – Assess value, develop cases, and prioritize stories, epics, and themes to ensure work focuses on those with maximum value that are aligned with product strategy;

• Ensure internal and external product stakeholders needs /expectations are met and promote transparency between all stakeholders;

• Keep updated with Agile/Scrum best practices and new trends.

Requirements:

What we need from you:

• At least 5 years commercial experience in similar role;

• Experience in conducting the discovery process;

• Demonstrated use of best practices, which will be a reference for others and sets the quality standards;

• Very good knowledge of spoken and written English (C1+);

• Eagerness to develop your skills and constantly seeks opportunities for improvement, new learnings & shows a strong "I can learn this" attitude;

• Being a team player focused on getting things done;

• Working experience in Agile/Scrum development environment;

• Experience in identifying and shaping business needs into product requirements through workshops, interviews, prototyping, and other techniques;

• Experience and knowledge of Agile software development processes;

• Strong intellectual curiosity to understand products, how they work, and how they solve client problems;

• Can focus on what’s important, synthesize complex information simply, and extract the most important insights.

• Experience with SaMD (Software as a Medical Device) projects is highly welcome.

We appreciate if you have:

• Strong interest in the topic of new technologies and healthcare;

• Experience working in healthcare projects.
